  "question": {
    "text": "Two blocks of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>&nbsp;are connected by a metal wire going over a smooth pulley as shown in the figure. The breaking stress of the metal wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;then what is the minimum radius of the wire which will not break<br />\r<br />\r<b><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0026_d05dafd40728.jpg\" style=\"width: 126px; height: 294px;\" /></u></b>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
