  "solution": {
    "text": "This is Atwood&#39;s machine. Let the tension in the wire be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> and acceleration of masses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>.<br /><br />Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math><br /><br />This gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>20</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mtext>g</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mtext>N</mtext></math>.<br /><br />Stress&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo></mrow><mtext>area</mtext></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>(given)</mtext></math><br /><br />Thus the minimum radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> should be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>200</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>03</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>0</mn><mtext>.</mtext><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>mm</mtext></math><br /><br /><b><u><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0026_d05dafd40728.jpg\" style=\"width: 126px; height: 294px;\" /></u></b>"
  }
